1
00:00:00,430 --> 00:00:01,410
Hi everyone.

2
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:03,917
I built a system that takes a video idea,

3
00:00:03,917 --> 00:00:06,147
plans and generates the shots,

4
00:00:06,147 --> 00:00:07,505
reviews the results,

5
00:00:07,505 --> 00:00:10,240
and turns everything into a finished video.

6
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,132
For this demo, I'll quickly show you

7
00:00:12,132 --> 00:00:14,810
the process and the final output.

8
00:00:14,810 --> 00:00:17,380
The process starts with a simple request.

9
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:18,658
Instead of giving Conductor

10
00:00:18,658 --> 00:00:20,644
a long prompt every time,

11
00:00:20,644 --> 00:00:22,629
I moved the recurring instructions

12
00:00:22,629 --> 00:00:23,891
into the workflow.

13
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:26,653
Now I can give it a short request,

14
00:00:26,653 --> 00:00:29,448
and the system handles the rest of the process.

15
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,001
The first thing the system does

16
00:00:32,001 --> 00:00:34,740
is look at this existing video library.

17
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:36,883
This library gives the system examples

18
00:00:36,883 --> 00:00:38,740
of different video styles,

19
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:42,000
pacing, transitions, and storytelling.

20
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,380
It uses those references as inspiration

21
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:45,935
to plan a new video,

22
00:00:45,935 --> 00:00:48,610
rather than copying one directly.

23
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:50,146
After reviewing the references,

24
00:00:50,146 --> 00:00:53,670
the system breaks the idea into individual shots.

25
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:55,720
For this video, it created four shots

26
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,019
with their own purpose, timing,

27
00:00:58,019 --> 00:01:00,640
copy, and visual direction.

28
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,716
Here, I'm showing three of them:

29
00:01:02,716 --> 00:01:03,645
the initial brief,

30
00:01:03,645 --> 00:01:04,655
the campaign idea,

31
00:01:04,655 --> 00:01:06,222
and how that idea expands

32
00:01:06,222 --> 00:01:08,550
into different marketing assets.

33
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:11,076
For this project, the system chose HyperFrames

34
00:01:11,076 --> 00:01:12,225
because the video needed

35
00:01:12,225 --> 00:01:14,954
precise text, UI, and layout

36
00:01:14,954 --> 00:01:17,000
instead of generative footage.

37
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,854
For other videos, it can use models

38
00:01:18,854 --> 00:01:20,050
available through Fal

39
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:21,559
when the shot needs things like

40
00:01:21,559 --> 00:01:24,390
cinematic movement or generated footage.

41
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:26,093
The idea is to choose the method

42
00:01:26,093 --> 00:01:27,869
that best fits the shot,

43
00:01:27,869 --> 00:01:29,518
instead of using the same model

44
00:01:29,518 --> 00:01:30,950
for everything.

45
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:32,832
Once the individual shots are ready,

46
00:01:32,832 --> 00:01:35,180
they're combined into the final video.

47
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:36,729
The workflow then checks things like

48
00:01:36,729 --> 00:01:38,981
timing, transitions, audio,

49
00:01:38,981 --> 00:01:40,200
and the final output

50
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,426
before considering the video complete.

51
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,474
For every finished video,

52
00:01:44,474 --> 00:01:45,902
the system creates its own

53
00:01:45,902 --> 00:01:47,870
reverse-engineering document.

54
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:49,905
This records how the video was made,

55
00:01:49,905 --> 00:01:52,157
including the prompts, structure,

56
00:01:52,157 --> 00:01:54,212
methods used, revisions,

57
00:01:54,212 --> 00:01:55,765
and key learnings.

58
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:57,738
The workflow also checks

59
00:01:57,738 --> 00:01:59,132
that this file exists

60
00:01:59,132 --> 00:02:02,010
before the video can be marked complete.

61
00:02:02,010 --> 00:02:03,471
And this is the final video

62
00:02:03,471 --> 00:02:05,290
produced through that workflow.

63
00:02:42,387 --> 00:02:43,752
The next phase I'm working on

64
00:02:43,752 --> 00:02:45,180
is human realism,

65
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:47,455
especially improving natural movement,

66
00:02:47,455 --> 00:02:48,872
hands, eye direction,

67
00:02:48,872 --> 00:02:50,767
and longer scenes with people.

68
00:02:50,767 --> 00:02:52,838
I'm keeping that research separate for now

69
00:02:52,838 --> 00:02:55,367
while I continue testing and improving it.
